h i get um  and i think it's you know it's because i  deal with the similar themes but i don't  usually think about themes when i'm  writing and i and they're probably  connections among the kinds of  characters  i use a lot of the same actors over and  over again and i guess there's visual  stuff that  you can link from one movie to another  way i mean a lot of things that i do the  same way every time  but it's just the way i like it and i  and i feel like it's a mistake for me  not to do it not to do that if i feel  like i if i feel like i have an idea  what the best  thing is for the story i would just want  to follow that  um even if it does mean that you know  people can tell it's me  is what else you said people who like  weird people i guess are more likely to  like my films and people who call people  weirdos  yeah i stand behind weird people it's  well it's it's kind of hard for me to  understand me and the way i phrase that  but i think i get it and i  and i agree with it you like people i  you know i mean i could i would say  people who call people weirdos not  people you like i i well i would say i  mean i'm sure i call people weirdos all  the time but i think  may but probably what i'm what i'm very  in a very odd way  and trying to get at is um that i don't  think i don't think  like people always refer to my movies as  quirky and they think the characters are  weird  and for me i can i can understand that  point of view about them but  almost every character in any movie i've  ever made is based on  somebody in real life or based on a  combination of real people  so even if i take it to a slightly odd  place  to me those are all real people and  they're characters that  that mean something to me beyond that  i'm not interested in the quirks i'm  interested in the whole  sum of the of the character if your  movies are weird people are weird  yeah the first idea for the movie  had nothing to do with the setting it  had to do with this one  character uh